# Cabin thermal-comfort recordings

Sensor recordings from the in-vehicle experiment of the PFL-TC paper (IEEE ETFA 2024).
One car was driven on two days in January 2024: on day 1 in the evening without
daylight, on day 2 in the afternoon with solar load. Each day is split into two
drives with different drivers. A Raspberry Pi polled the sensors about every
3.7 s (7–8 samples per minute).

`cabin_comfort.csv` has 2,115 rows, one per reading. It was produced from the
raw Excel export with [`scripts/prepare_data.py`](../scripts/prepare_data.py),
which keeps only the measurement sheet, renames the columns and replaces the
driver codes with pseudonymous indices.

| drive_id | day | driver_id | samples | duration | conditions |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 1 | 1 | 1 | 548 | 43 min | evening, city and highway, no daylight |
| 2 | 1 | 2 | 435 | 38 min | evening, no daylight |
| 3 | 2 | 1 | 557 | 47 min | afternoon, solar load |
| 4 | 2 | 3 | 575 | 50 min | afternoon, solar load |

## Columns

| Column | Unit | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `timestamp` | local time | time of the reading |
| `day` | – | recording day (1 = 1 Jan 2024, 2 = 2 Jan 2024) |
| `drive_id` | – | continuous drive with one driver (1–4) |
| `driver_id` | – | pseudonymous driver index (1–3); driver 1 drove on both days |
| `elapsed_s` | s | time since the start of the drive |
| `ambient_temp_c` | °C | outside air temperature (sensor outside the window) |
| `cabin_temp_c` | °C | cabin air temperature (dashboard, next to the HVAC unit) |
| `cabin_rh_pct` | % | cabin relative humidity |
| `light_intensity` | sensor reading | uncalibrated light-sensor value on the dashboard, used as a proxy for solar load ("Solar Load" in the paper) |
| `met` | met | metabolic rate; constant 1.0 in this release |
| `clo` | clo | clothing insulation; constant 0.5 in this release |
| `z1_skin_temp_c`, `z2_skin_temp_c`, `z3_skin_temp_c` | °C | local skin temperature in zone 1 (driver), 2 (front passenger) and 3 (rear bench) |
| `z1_rh_pct`, `z2_rh_pct`, `z3_rh_pct` | % | relative humidity in each zone |
| `z1_vote`, `z2_vote`, `z3l_vote`, `z3r_vote` | −3 … +3 | thermal sensation vote of the occupant of each seat on the ASHRAE 7-point scale (−3 cold, 0 neutral, +3 hot), recorded by hand roughly every 3 minutes; the paper calls these values PMV. `z3r_vote` is empty on day 2 (seat unoccupied) |

## Things to know before using the data

* **No HVAC set-point log.** The paper's target, the set temperature, is not part of
  this release. The code therefore derives a per-occupant *neutral temperature*
  from the comfort votes by default (see the main README). If you have set-point
  logs, add them as columns and set `target.mode: column`.
* **Zones are seats, not persons.** The driver changes between drives (`driver_id`)
  and passengers also changed seats, so a zone's occupant is not always the same person.
* **`met` and `clo` are constant** and carry no information in this release.
* **One sensor glitch**: `z3_rh_pct` reads 6 % once (day 1, 17:53:25). The pipeline
  masks values outside physically plausible ranges and interpolates them.
* Votes change about every 50 samples, so neighbouring rows are near-duplicates.
  Split the data in time (as the code does), not at random.
